parent;"></div></figure>
<p>This can be reflected using a parent array, where <code>parent[i]</code>=
 stores the parent of person <code>i</code>. This parent array is discussed=
 later.</p>
<p>Now that we have a way to represent communities, let=E2=80=99s discuss h=
ow the <code>union</code> and <code>find</code> functions would work in mor=
e detail.</p>
<p><strong>Union</strong><br>
Consider the previous example of 5 people. Let=E2=80=99s say we want to con=
nect persons 1 and 4 (i.e., <code>union(1, 4)</code>):</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a directed graph illustrating a union opera=
