courses/coding-patterns/graphs/merging-communities/image-13-07-6-BQLPJMHJ.s=
vg" style=3D"color: transparent;"></div></figure>
<p>This way, everyone originally in the second community is indirectly conn=
ected to person 0, making person 0 the representative of all nodes.</p>
<p>Note that if rep_x and rep_y are the same person, then they belong to th=
e same community, in which case we don=E2=80=99t need to merge anything.</p=
>
<p><strong>Find</strong><br>
The <code>find</code> function should return the representative of the comm=
unity a person is in:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
